# tinted-dircolors
# Scheme name: Lumina Aurora Light
# Scheme author: Razik Ikhlef (https://github.com/RazikSF)
# Template author: tinted-dircolors (local), modelled on seebi/dircolors-solarized
#
# Portions Copyright (c) 2020 Sebastian Tramp, MIT License
# https://github.com/seebi/dircolors-solarized/blob/master/LICENSE
#
# Based on the GNU coreutils dircolors database (dircolors -p):
# Copyright (C) 1996-2025 Free Software Foundation, Inc.
# Copying and distribution of this file, with or without modification,
# are permitted provided the copyright notice and this notice are preserved.
#
# Colors are 24-bit truecolor (38;2;R;G;B / 48;2;R;G;B) taken from the scheme,
# so they do not depend on the terminal's 16/256-color palette.
#
# Usage: eval "$(dircolors -b this-file)"

# Terminals that get colors at all
COLORTERM ?*
TERM Eterm
TERM ansi
TERM *color*
TERM con[0-9]*x[0-9]*
TERM cons25
TERM console
TERM cygwin
TERM *direct*
TERM dtterm
TERM gnome
TERM hurd
TERM jfbterm
TERM konsole
TERM kterm
TERM linux
TERM linux-c
TERM mlterm
TERM putty
TERM rxvt*
TERM screen*
TERM st
TERM terminator
TERM tmux*
TERM vt100
TERM vt220
TERM xterm*

